  "live_records": {
    "q-40648": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40648",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the subspace spanned by $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nIn our case, $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={29}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{29}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
