    "q-95188": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95188",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the subspace spanned by $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nIn our case, $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(21)^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}16 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
