    "q-95199": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95199",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the plane whose parametric equation is $r=sv+tw$, where\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nNotice that the plane $r=sv+tw$ is actually the subspace $\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}.$ \nHence, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95199-a",
